WEBVTT

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:03.600
"Setting Up

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:03.600
Please wait juuust a little longer."

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:06.940
I've registered you in our database.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:10.390
Now you're formally a member of the Verbalism Club.

00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:16.040
"Authentication"

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:20.110
You stay there and monitor the pilot of the red vector.

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:25.750
Also, I have something to supply all of you with.

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:27.520
What're those?

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:31.060
Portable communication terminals developed by Deava.

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:33.090
Even in an area affected by the M.J.B.K.,

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:36.700
with these, we can stay in contact over independent channels.

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:38.900
We call them Aquariphones.

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:41.740
Huh? What'd you just call them?

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:43.360
Aquariphones.

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:50.710
A-Aren't you going to turn it on?

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:52.110
I'm not using it right now.

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:54.580
Oh, come on, seriously?

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:56.920
If it's not on, we can't contact you.

00:00:56.920 --> 00:00:58.410
Oh, you can't?

00:00:59.590 --> 00:01:02.920
Could it be... Akira...

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:04.950
--You have no friends?
--You have no friends?

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:13.070
Commander, what sort of lethal powers is this Aquariphone hiding?

00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:14.440
It's not hiding any.

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:16.840
Honestly, this girl's no better...

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:20.080
You jerk. Maia can't help it.

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:23.280
She's been cooped up by this
Sougon guy ever since she was little.

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:26.310
She was <i>never</i> allowed outside.

00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:27.920
Right?

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:29.620
Y-Yeah...

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:31.320
But, at long last, she has awakened to justice,

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:34.360
and has resolved to fight alongside us!

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:36.790
Just brings you to tears, don't it?

00:01:36.790 --> 00:01:39.830
I'm on your side, Maia!

00:01:39.830 --> 00:01:42.160
Uh, sure...

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:43.330
Also...

00:01:43.330 --> 00:01:45.320
Pardon me!

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:52.330
We have another new member joining the Verbalism Club, as well.

00:01:53.810 --> 00:01:56.680
Hello! I'm Karan Uminagi!

00:01:56.680 --> 00:02:01.670
My dream's to be an idol who can give everyone courage!

00:02:05.450 --> 00:02:07.980
"Dream"

00:02:08.390 --> 00:02:12.860
At one time, man was one with the world of truth.

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:17.960
But the written word brought forth prosperity and suffering.

00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:27.680
<i>Oh, "yamai-dare," darlin' darlin,'</i> <i>you're a divine crown</i>

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:33.680
<i>The kanji for "love" and "grief " look very similar</i>

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:39.050
<i>When I realized that, dawn suddenly broke</i>

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:44.860
<i>The air was filled with so much</i> <i>silence that "blue" "fought"</i>

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:51.200
<i>When suddenly you slid in to the right of me</i>

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:54.070
<i>Rippling with a clatter</i>

00:02:54.070 --> 00:02:57.040
<i>and tangled in red thread</i>

00:02:57.040 --> 00:03:01.910
<i>and a 39-degree fever of passion</i>

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:07.380
<i>Oh, "yamai-dare," darlin' darlin,'</i> <i>you're a divine crown</i>

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:13.420
<i>A crown worn on high with pride</i>

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:18.890
<i>Oh, "yamai-dare," darlin' darlin,'</i> <i>"soothe" my hidden "heart below"</i>

00:03:18.890 --> 00:03:24.900
<i>Its form is too much to handle right now</i>

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:27.800
<i>God's wisdom, the "h" in "her"</i>

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:30.570
<i>With a tearful, feverish gaze</i>

00:03:30.570 --> 00:03:33.470
<i>let's stand side by side</i> <i>and look at tomorrow's moon</i>

00:03:33.470 --> 00:03:36.310
<i>(Let's stand side by side</i> <i>and look at tomorrow's moon)</i>

00:03:36.310 --> 00:03:43.740
<i>The things you can do are so striking</i>

00:03:48.490 --> 00:03:51.550
"Resound! A Dream for Me Alone"

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:55.560
We, the little pigs, want to build sturdy houses

00:03:55.560 --> 00:03:58.670
that will stand strong even if a wolf comes.

00:03:58.670 --> 00:04:03.740
But this lake is important to us swans.

00:04:03.740 --> 00:04:07.140
That's why we ask you to leave.
But have no fear.

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:08.480
--You'll be compensated.
--What is this?

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:10.610
They're rehearsing for our reading theater.

00:04:10.610 --> 00:04:15.280
The script they're doing now is
<i>The Three Little Pigs in Swan Lake.</i>

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:17.920
It's a Shirobaco original.

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:22.590
Shirobaco isn't just a café. It's also a place for the Verbalism Club to perform.

00:04:22.590 --> 00:04:26.830
We do reading theater, plays, and even mini-concerts.

00:04:26.830 --> 00:04:31.030
There are even regular customers who come just to see it.

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:36.440
Give it up already, Swan.

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:37.970
Y-You're...

00:04:37.970 --> 00:04:42.210
By speaking in front of people, they develop their Verbalism Ability.

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:44.610
That brings out the power of the written word

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:47.220
and gives them the power to face the M.J.B.K.

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:49.880
That's the reason for the
Verbalism Club's activities.

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:53.390
I think you've seen just about everything now.

00:04:53.390 --> 00:04:56.520
If there's anywhere I haven't shown you yet...

00:04:56.520 --> 00:04:58.990
Ah! The hangar.

00:04:58.990 --> 00:05:01.860
I think you've seen it, but would you like to go there?

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:03.330
Yes.

00:05:03.330 --> 00:05:06.300
A new vector arrived today.

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:10.000
I told you, I can't have you doing that.

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:12.310
Oh, don't be such a stick in the mud.

00:05:12.310 --> 00:05:14.740
Okay, Karan. Do your next pose.

00:05:14.740 --> 00:05:15.910
Okay!

00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:17.850
Give me a brighter smile!

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:20.250
Okay!

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:21.820
I've asked you to stop.

00:05:21.820 --> 00:05:24.650
Um, manager, who is this?

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:27.690
What? We have a contract, you know?

00:05:27.690 --> 00:05:29.660
That's not the point.

00:05:32.830 --> 00:05:36.230
Huh? Because she wants to market her daughter as an idol--

00:05:36.230 --> 00:05:38.600
that's the only reason she let her daughter join the Verbalism Club?

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:42.040
At the moment, our existence is a secret from the public,

00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:46.940
but the manager does say she plans to disclose everything once it's over.

00:05:48.040 --> 00:05:50.850
When that happens, she'll also be talking about Karan,

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:53.580
so the plan is to go big with her then.

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:56.180
As the idol who saved the world.

00:05:56.180 --> 00:05:58.750
That's a novel angle to take.

00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:03.760
So she was doing a photo shoot in preparation for that. Makes sense.

00:06:03.760 --> 00:06:05.730
It all seems so complicated.

00:06:05.730 --> 00:06:09.960
We contacted Karan after discovering her Verbalism Ability, though.

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:11.800
Well, I don't see a problem.

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:15.940
We're all in the Verbalism Club to pursue our own dreams.

00:06:15.940 --> 00:06:17.140
Dreams?

00:06:17.140 --> 00:06:18.310
Y-Yeah.

00:06:18.310 --> 00:06:24.050
W-We each... have our own dreams... which involve our voices...

00:06:24.050 --> 00:06:28.080
Like Hayato, who dreams of giving totally badass political speeches.

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:31.620
Though I think it's a bit weird he uses it to power a campaigning car.

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:34.590
They let me borrow it free of charge outside of the election period.

00:06:34.590 --> 00:06:36.560
I can't complain.

00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:38.460
Sorry for the wait.

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:41.000
Huh? Why you, Maia?

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:44.500
She's going to be doing live-in work here starting today.

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:46.500
It's a pleasure to work with you.

00:06:46.500 --> 00:06:48.470
I've got a bad feeling.

00:06:48.470 --> 00:06:51.570
Why should I have to take that kind of lip from you?

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:54.140
Shoko, get me the usual.

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:56.310
Ah! Sure thing!

00:06:56.310 --> 00:06:57.980
Sorry for the wait.

00:06:57.980 --> 00:07:01.980
Shirobaco's famous
Bags Under the Eyes Latte.

00:07:01.980 --> 00:07:05.190
Oh, my! Mr. Customer, your eyes are all red.

00:07:05.190 --> 00:07:07.420
Were you up working all night, perhaps?

00:07:07.420 --> 00:07:09.290
Oh, you could tell?

00:07:09.290 --> 00:07:12.160
Here, drink this and it'll perk you right up!

00:07:14.360 --> 00:07:16.530
Maia, could you do that?

00:07:16.530 --> 00:07:19.870
I've committed the manual to memory. Yes, flawlessly.

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:22.670
Then I'll have a Bags Under the Eyes Latte.

00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:24.440
Sorry for the wait.

00:07:24.440 --> 00:07:26.870
Shirobaco's famous
Bags Under the Eyes Latte.

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:31.310
Mr. Customer, your eyes are all red.

00:07:31.310 --> 00:07:34.150
Huh? Wait... Isn't this a bit off?

00:07:34.150 --> 00:07:36.450
Were you up working all night, perhaps?

00:07:36.450 --> 00:07:37.980
Hey, wait... Er...

00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:42.360
Rest in peace.

00:07:42.360 --> 00:07:44.790
She's not even getting the lines right anymore!

00:07:44.790 --> 00:07:46.860
You just have to complain over every little thing.

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:49.330
We <i>are</i> technically a secret organization.

00:07:49.330 --> 00:07:54.400
Karan, you'll start participating fully in Verbalism Club lessons tomorrow.

00:07:54.400 --> 00:07:57.510
Rest well today so you're in good shape for tomorrow.

00:07:57.510 --> 00:07:59.010
Yep!

00:07:59.010 --> 00:08:02.140
Everyone, it's a pleasure to be joining you.

00:08:02.140 --> 00:08:03.980
Yeah, pleased to have you too.

00:08:03.980 --> 00:08:05.880
L-Likewise.

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:07.720
Pleased to have you.

00:08:07.720 --> 00:08:09.350
We're going, Karan.

00:08:09.350 --> 00:08:10.840
Okay.

00:08:11.920 --> 00:08:13.920
What a sweet little kid.

00:08:13.920 --> 00:08:17.230
Yeah, I will acknowledge her mother's taught her well.

00:08:17.230 --> 00:08:21.500
Hey, Shoko, how have you been teaching Maia, anyway?

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:24.560
Huh? I just told her how to do it normally.

00:08:25.770 --> 00:08:27.500
Akira's gone.

00:08:27.500 --> 00:08:31.340
--Oh, shoot!
--Maia? Where are you going?

00:08:35.110 --> 00:08:39.570
Akira Kaibuki...
Monitoring him is my duty.

00:08:40.550 --> 00:08:43.380
Another failed audition...

00:08:43.380 --> 00:08:46.050
My little girl's not good at singing.

00:08:46.050 --> 00:08:48.390
Uminagi, yours is really something.

00:08:48.390 --> 00:08:50.730
It's thanks to the strict way she raises her.

00:08:50.730 --> 00:08:53.390
You even limit the amount of TV she can watch, right?

00:08:53.390 --> 00:08:55.900
It's all for her dreams, so how could I not?

00:08:55.900 --> 00:09:01.770
I want to make absolutely sure Karan reaches her dream of being a top idol.

00:09:06.370 --> 00:09:08.780
Wow, amazing.

00:09:08.780 --> 00:09:11.910
I see. So that's what your real voice sounds like.

00:09:13.750 --> 00:09:18.290
Oh, you're from the
Verbalism Club. Hello there.

00:09:18.290 --> 00:09:19.890
That's sickening.

00:09:19.890 --> 00:09:21.090
Teehee.

00:09:21.090 --> 00:09:25.060
That smile you have plastered to your face is sickening.

00:09:25.060 --> 00:09:29.460
I get told at the auditions that it's a nice smile.

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:32.500
Are you smiling to be told how nice your smile is?

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:34.440
No wonder it seems so fake.

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:36.840
What's your problem?

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:39.910
You can't save anything with a false smile and a false voice.

00:09:39.910 --> 00:09:43.340
You... Are you planning to get in my way?

00:09:43.340 --> 00:09:44.970
What's that supposed to mean?

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:48.450
What do you know?

00:09:48.450 --> 00:09:51.590
I'm going to be an idol!
This is for my dream!

00:09:51.590 --> 00:09:53.280
You were being fake again just now.

00:09:54.590 --> 00:09:58.360
Is this dream you're talking about really <i>your</i> dream?

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:05.870
Verbalize.

00:10:03.970 --> 00:10:04.830
"Verbalism"

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:07.940
Rejoice.

00:10:07.940 --> 00:10:10.770
I shall now set you free.

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:14.110
"Dream"

00:10:19.880 --> 00:10:21.940
Yume!

00:10:25.350 --> 00:10:27.990
<i>Un, deux, trois. Un, deux, trois.</i>

00:10:27.990 --> 00:10:29.690
<i>--Un, deux, trois.</i>
--What's his problem?

00:10:28.360 --> 00:10:30.120
"Apply Now for the Summer Session

00:10:28.360 --> 00:10:30.120
Narita Ballet Classroom

00:10:28.360 --> 00:10:30.120
Give your children a dream."

00:10:29.690 --> 00:10:32.960
--Okay, keep it up like that.
--I'm working hard for my dream here.

00:10:32.960 --> 00:10:35.030
What's wrong with that?

00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:39.370
Your back is a little crooked there.
Try to straighten up.

00:10:39.370 --> 00:10:41.500
What are you letting your eyes stray for?

00:10:41.500 --> 00:10:44.230
Do you think you can become an idol like that?

00:10:45.840 --> 00:10:47.480
It's your dream, isn't it?

00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:50.680
Be more desperate about it!

00:10:50.680 --> 00:10:53.340
M-Mom...

00:11:04.030 --> 00:11:08.360
Yume. Yume. Yume. Yume...

00:11:10.930 --> 00:11:15.160
I can dream all I want, but I'll never be a pro!

00:11:16.240 --> 00:11:18.840
No, I could never submit work like this!

00:11:18.840 --> 00:11:20.570
I'll never be an artist!

00:11:20.570 --> 00:11:23.910
Someday, I'll go see a movie with Kokone!

00:11:23.910 --> 00:11:25.850
That's my dream!

00:11:25.850 --> 00:11:28.720
Hayato, let's go for a drive.

00:11:28.720 --> 00:11:31.220
Make my dream come true!

00:11:31.220 --> 00:11:32.450
Manager!

00:11:32.450 --> 00:11:35.690
Call Kaibuki and Tsukigane back here at once.

00:11:35.690 --> 00:11:37.260
I'll boot up the system.

00:11:37.260 --> 00:11:38.890
R-Right!

00:11:40.360 --> 00:11:41.850
"Tsutomu Domon

00:11:40.360 --> 00:11:41.850
Akira Kaibuki

00:11:40.360 --> 00:11:41.850
Hayato Kujyo"

00:11:42.030 --> 00:11:43.600
I-It's no good...

00:11:43.600 --> 00:11:47.130
Akira's... ph-phone isn't on...

00:11:47.130 --> 00:11:50.260
That dunce. I told him to turn it on.

00:11:51.770 --> 00:11:53.970
It's ringing.

00:11:53.970 --> 00:11:56.270
That's Maia's.

00:11:58.280 --> 00:12:00.610
Where... is this?

00:12:04.220 --> 00:12:06.080
"Dream"

00:12:08.620 --> 00:12:09.890
I'm getting off.

00:12:09.890 --> 00:12:13.390
Like your brat could ever be a ballerina!

00:12:13.390 --> 00:12:14.900
She's a pudgy little thing!

00:12:14.900 --> 00:12:17.260
My daughter will make her dreams come true!

00:12:17.260 --> 00:12:20.270
Mom! Mom, be strong!

00:12:20.270 --> 00:12:23.900
You must become an idol.
Absolutely. No matter what happens.

00:12:23.900 --> 00:12:26.440
Right. I'll work real hard!

00:12:26.440 --> 00:12:29.080
You absolutely must become a top idol.

00:12:29.080 --> 00:12:31.610
I●●●

00:12:31.610 --> 00:12:34.280
I'll be an idol... a star.

00:12:34.280 --> 00:12:38.520
The center of attention, standing on a shining stage.

00:12:38.520 --> 00:12:41.150
I want to sing my heart out.

00:12:44.830 --> 00:12:48.090
"Dream"

00:12:48.160 --> 00:12:51.630
Yes, it's not too late.

00:12:51.630 --> 00:12:55.300
This is what that Sakurako lady was talking about.

00:12:55.300 --> 00:12:57.470
I just need an opportunity.

00:12:57.340 --> 00:13:00.110
"Apply Now for the Summer Session

00:12:57.340 --> 00:13:00.110
Narita Ballet Classroom

00:12:57.340 --> 00:13:00.110
Give your children a dream."

00:12:57.470 --> 00:12:59.640
Wait for me, Mom!

00:13:01.980 --> 00:13:03.470
Karan?

00:13:06.510 --> 00:13:10.020
"Closed Due to Emergency

00:13:06.510 --> 00:13:10.020
Sorry. Come again another time!"

00:13:06.980 --> 00:13:10.050
Are our crafts still not repaired?

00:13:10.050 --> 00:13:11.490
Waiting's a pain.

00:13:11.490 --> 00:13:13.720
They may be dinged up a bit, but they'll probably still work.

00:13:13.720 --> 00:13:15.160
Let's get out there, Hayato.

00:13:15.160 --> 00:13:16.360
Not a chance.

00:13:16.360 --> 00:13:18.350
Then... I'll go!

00:13:19.830 --> 00:13:22.300
Karan? What are you doing here?

00:13:23.300 --> 00:13:25.830
Let me fight!

00:13:25.830 --> 00:13:28.070
I'll fight!

00:13:28.070 --> 00:13:30.370
But you can't so suddenly...

00:13:30.370 --> 00:13:32.670
You still haven't started training.

00:13:36.540 --> 00:13:38.040
Akira?

00:13:39.480 --> 00:13:42.720
I'll go with her.

00:13:42.720 --> 00:13:44.350
I will save the world.

00:13:44.350 --> 00:13:47.150
Will we need your voice for that?

00:13:47.150 --> 00:13:48.850
Let me hear it.

00:13:51.830 --> 00:13:53.920
Deava System, activate!

00:13:52.890 --> 00:13:53.160
"Closed Today Due to Emergency"

00:13:56.830 --> 00:13:58.320
Verbalize!

00:13:58.930 --> 00:13:59.500
"Verbalism"

00:13:59.500 --> 00:14:02.770
Vector exit lane link system operational.

00:14:07.440 --> 00:14:10.010
Karan. Karan, where are you?

00:14:10.010 --> 00:14:11.950
Where are you, Karan?

00:14:27.430 --> 00:14:29.360
Come here, we're going to Gattai.

00:14:34.440 --> 00:14:37.040
Sousei Gattai, bloom beautifully...

00:14:37.040 --> 00:14:39.910
...Aquarion!

00:14:56.390 --> 00:14:58.230
"Rin"

00:14:56.920 --> 00:14:58.460
Rin!

00:14:58.460 --> 00:15:02.090
Yume. Yume! Yume!!

00:15:14.440 --> 00:15:16.140
The kid's not half bad!

00:15:16.140 --> 00:15:20.450
But ordinary weapons can't finish off an M.J.B.K.

00:15:20.450 --> 00:15:24.290
Yes, there's something we need...
Some means to win.

00:15:24.290 --> 00:15:26.120
Yume!

00:15:27.690 --> 00:15:30.790
Yume...

00:15:30.790 --> 00:15:32.490
I have to shake it off!

00:15:35.960 --> 00:15:37.770
Become an idol.

00:15:37.770 --> 00:15:41.040
A beautiful, sparkling top idol!

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:43.000
I must become an idol.

00:15:43.000 --> 00:15:46.640
I'll stand on the stage and sing for everyone.

00:15:46.640 --> 00:15:48.010
Stop.

00:15:48.010 --> 00:15:51.480
An idol. I want to become a number one idol

00:15:51.480 --> 00:15:53.280
and be the focus of everyone's admiration.

00:15:53.280 --> 00:15:55.320
Stop it! I don't want to hear it!

00:15:55.320 --> 00:15:57.950
Karan's vital gauge is dropping rapidly.

00:15:57.950 --> 00:15:59.720
She'll be in danger if this keeps up!

00:15:59.720 --> 00:16:00.990
It was too much for her after all!

00:16:00.990 --> 00:16:02.520
Commander, I'll go.

00:16:02.520 --> 00:16:03.720
I can't authorize that.

00:16:03.720 --> 00:16:07.130
You going out in a damaged vector isn't going to get us through this.

00:16:07.130 --> 00:16:08.360
But...!

00:16:08.360 --> 00:16:09.960
I want to be an idol!

00:16:09.960 --> 00:16:12.570
An idol who can sing, who can dance, who can do anything!

00:16:12.570 --> 00:16:15.870
No! I don't want to hear any more!

00:16:15.870 --> 00:16:18.540
No, listen.

00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:23.480
And see for yourself... the reality behind the dream that's crushing you.

00:16:28.750 --> 00:16:30.580
K-Karan!

00:16:31.590 --> 00:16:33.390
I'm detecting a person in front of Shirobaco.

00:16:33.390 --> 00:16:35.190
Who is it at a time like this?

00:16:36.720 --> 00:16:40.190
I-It's Karan's mother.

00:16:40.190 --> 00:16:42.660
Let her through.

00:16:42.660 --> 00:16:43.660
But...!

00:16:43.660 --> 00:16:46.770
A voice must be directed to someone.

00:16:46.700 --> 00:16:49.530
"Closed Due to Emergency

00:16:46.700 --> 00:16:49.530
Sorry. Come again another time!"

00:16:46.770 --> 00:16:49.240
Karan. You're in there, aren't you?

00:16:52.870 --> 00:16:55.840
P-Please, come with me.

00:16:55.840 --> 00:16:57.380
Karan!

00:16:57.380 --> 00:16:58.410
Mom!

00:16:58.410 --> 00:17:00.010
Come back, Karan.

00:17:00.010 --> 00:17:02.380
I need you.

00:17:02.380 --> 00:17:06.180
In order... In order to make my dream come true.

00:17:14.630 --> 00:17:27.880
"Danger"

00:17:18.800 --> 00:17:22.400
Mom... I knew.

00:17:22.400 --> 00:17:27.980
That it wasn't my dream you wanted to make come true... it was your own.

00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:30.140
Karan, you...

00:17:30.140 --> 00:17:34.950
The one who wants to be an idol is you, not me, isn't it, Mom?

00:17:34.950 --> 00:17:40.080
But because you couldn't, you entrusted your dream to me.

00:17:41.460 --> 00:17:42.950
Yume.

00:17:56.100 --> 00:17:57.470
Yume!

00:17:57.470 --> 00:17:59.270
It's the same for ballet!

00:17:59.270 --> 00:18:02.780
The one who really wants to dance is you, right, Mom?

00:18:02.780 --> 00:18:06.310
Yume...

00:18:06.310 --> 00:18:08.420
But still...

00:18:08.420 --> 00:18:10.850
I'm not your replacement.

00:18:11.850 --> 00:18:13.790
I'm Karan Uminagi!

00:18:13.790 --> 00:18:16.860
I'm my own person!

00:18:16.160 --> 00:18:17.850
"Person"

00:18:23.660 --> 00:18:27.370
It's the same as with Akira...
She called up a k-kanji!

00:18:27.370 --> 00:18:29.040
That's right.

00:18:29.040 --> 00:18:32.710
When what should be spoken is given voice at the right time,

00:18:32.710 --> 00:18:36.380
it gives power to the word and can change reality.

00:18:36.380 --> 00:18:40.550
The right time. The right place.
That is what gives Verbalism power!

00:18:38.610 --> 00:18:40.640
"Dream"

00:18:41.180 --> 00:18:42.550
"Ephemeral"

00:18:43.050 --> 00:18:46.190
My true feelings, which I could never speak.

00:18:46.190 --> 00:18:48.360
I was finally able to say it.

00:18:48.360 --> 00:18:50.860
The dreams of people are an ephemeral thing.

00:18:50.860 --> 00:18:55.960
And so, all the more, there is reason to risk everything for that one moment.

00:18:55.960 --> 00:18:57.500
Unleash it.

00:18:57.500 --> 00:19:00.470
This is amazing! It feels so good!

00:19:00.470 --> 00:19:02.830
Yume! Yume!

00:19:23.260 --> 00:19:25.660
Oh, I see now...

00:19:25.660 --> 00:19:29.720
My own ephemeral dream ended long ago, didn't it?

00:19:30.060 --> 00:19:32.160
"Ephemeral"

00:19:51.120 --> 00:19:53.050
I'm sorry, Karan.

00:19:53.050 --> 00:19:57.220
I... I tied you down with my dream.

00:19:58.560 --> 00:20:00.730
No, it's fine.

00:20:00.730 --> 00:20:05.600
I've realized wanting to become an idol wasn't my real dream.

00:20:07.570 --> 00:20:09.900
I have a dream.

00:20:09.900 --> 00:20:14.640
A dream all of my own.
I... I want to be a voice actor!

00:20:17.240 --> 00:20:19.040
Work hard at it.

00:20:21.550 --> 00:20:23.450
Why must you be so noisy?

00:20:23.450 --> 00:20:26.050
Maia's still missing, isn't she?

00:20:27.420 --> 00:20:30.320
Commander, I have an idea.

00:20:33.990 --> 00:20:36.430
You're taking this awfully easy.

00:20:36.430 --> 00:20:40.000
Even after the M.J.B.K. you made yourself was destroyed.

00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:44.500
Nesta Verbalism Ability Lab Head,
Shintaro Hayashi.

00:20:44.500 --> 00:20:47.270
Oh, it's the young master.

00:20:47.270 --> 00:20:49.940
I've told you not to call me that.

00:20:49.940 --> 00:20:52.810
It's not that we're making M.J.B.K.s.

00:20:52.810 --> 00:20:56.910
What's making them are the ampules that turn kanji into M.J.B.K.s.

00:20:58.620 --> 00:21:00.750
If you have time on your hands, help me out.

00:21:00.750 --> 00:21:02.920
There's something I want to make.

00:21:02.920 --> 00:21:05.090
You seem more serious than usual.

00:21:05.090 --> 00:21:06.960
Of course I've gotten serious.

00:21:08.260 --> 00:21:11.530
This is to take Maia back.

00:21:11.530 --> 00:21:14.370
Where should I go?

00:21:15.800 --> 00:21:18.440
Maia Tsukigane.

00:21:18.440 --> 00:21:22.140
If you're there, answer me. Maia Tsukigane.

00:21:22.140 --> 00:21:25.880
A voice... I hear a voice.

00:21:25.880 --> 00:21:29.020
Aren't you there, Maia Tsukigane?

00:21:29.020 --> 00:21:30.880
Akira Kaibuki.

00:21:35.860 --> 00:21:39.020
Looks like your voice reached her.

00:21:49.840 --> 00:21:51.640
What do you want?

00:21:51.640 --> 00:21:53.630
Carry your cell phone.

00:21:55.910 --> 00:21:58.750
You're a pain to deal with.

00:21:58.750 --> 00:22:00.510
I entered my number.

00:22:00.510 --> 00:22:04.520
If you need something, call me.
Before it becomes a pain to deal with.

00:22:04.520 --> 00:22:09.520
They got mad at me, too. I'll do you all the favor of leaving it on in the future.

00:22:09.520 --> 00:22:13.890
You act so self-important.
Who do you think you are?

00:22:13.890 --> 00:22:15.390
I'm the savior.

00:22:37.420 --> 00:22:40.890
<i>Je-Je t'aime communication</i>

00:22:40.890 --> 00:22:50.890
<i>Oh, you aren't making a bit of</i> <i>eye contact with me while you talk</i>

00:22:50.930 --> 00:23:00.140
<i>Are you texting some far-off</i> <i>neighboring world or something?</i>

00:23:00.140 --> 00:23:05.270
<i>Because this isn't communication at all</i>

00:23:07.210 --> 00:23:13.750
<i>You'd at least understand that much</i>

00:23:13.750 --> 00:23:19.760
<i>even if the times suddenly changed, right?</i>

00:23:19.760 --> 00:23:23.760
<i>Give me je t'aime communication sometimes</i>

00:23:23.760 --> 00:23:27.170
<i>Look at me, answer me, and tell me</i>

00:23:27.170 --> 00:23:33.670
<i>I mean, this is practically</i> <i>like talking to a computer</i>

00:23:33.670 --> 00:23:36.680
<i>A-Adieu application</i>

00:23:36.680 --> 00:23:43.320
<i>Even if it means staying lonely</i> <i>in my heart, if it'll connect us</i>

00:23:43.320 --> 00:23:49.690
<i>then, please, at least show</i> <i>your smile to me alone</i>

00:23:50.990 --> 00:24:06.010
"Next Episode Preview"

00:23:51.320 --> 00:23:53.460
Hey, have you heard of Tanabata?

00:23:53.460 --> 00:23:54.760
It's one of the five festivals in Japan, right?

00:23:54.760 --> 00:23:55.800
<i>T-Tanzaku...</i>

00:23:55.800 --> 00:23:56.700
What about <i>tanzaku</i>?

00:23:56.700 --> 00:23:58.800
I-If you write your wish on one, it might come true...

00:23:58.800 --> 00:23:59.870
Is that true?

00:23:59.870 --> 00:24:02.540
Yeah, you find a salaryman who looks like he's doing well,

00:24:02.540 --> 00:24:03.770
and you hang the <i>tanzaku</i> on him.

00:24:03.770 --> 00:24:05.970
Got it. I'll go hang one.

00:24:05.970 --> 00:24:08.110
"Let Fly! An Arrow that Pierces the Heart."

00:24:06.510 --> 00:24:08.510
"Episode 4: Let Fly! An Arrow

00:24:06.510 --> 00:24:08.510
that Pierces the Heart"

00:24:08.110 --> 00:24:10.370
L-L-Look forward to it...?
